{"title":"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #8</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the entire figure shown is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58cf809859c6a38fdcbcf23b4916fb3bb3d781e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 16 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 32 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 24 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see all of the right triangles are equivalent because their legs are all equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we only need to find the area of one triangle, and then multiply that by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>From triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, its area is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a9720fb4377c946ebe08f04baeb13f77523153ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times 4 = 2 \\times 4 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the total area would be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4ab861dd9c13483b70c0efcb8151476ce4068065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 3 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"132\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 